14.2 In the app

The Result
Open a completed count from the Count tab. The card at the top leads with what was counted, then what was short and over, in units and at cost. The sentence ends with what changed: for the demo’s count at Showcase 1, “11 of 13 matched (85%)… Completed 26 Sep. Stock adjusted for 1 product; 1 left as it was.”







Below it:

when the count was completed, and what it covered;
where expected stock came from (Jholok’s ledger, or the books);
who counted, and who approved and why;
the count’s part of the activity log, and whether it’s intact.

If the phone hasn’t been backed up since, a reminder says “This count is only on this phone until it’s backed up” (chapter 15).
Then the lists:

Stock adjusted and Left unchanged;
where they apply, the tags not found or found outside the books (Chapter 11), what was off the shelf (Chapter 12), single earrings found, and pieces not in the catalogue (Chapter 10);
entries made after completion;
products not counted, and the products that matched.










Share the report
Tap the Export button at the top and choose:

Count report (PDF): the full report, for printing or keeping;
Lines and log (CSV): every line of the count, and its log, for a spreadsheet.








The owner confirms each time, with Face ID or the owner PIN (until People is set up, Face ID or the phone’s passcode). The first time, Jholok asks for the shop’s name and address, to print at the top. The files are made only for sharing: once the share sheet closes, Jholok deletes its copies.
Settings → Export also has Count results: every line of every completed count, in one spreadsheet. While a count is open, exports that would show its stock wait until it’s reviewed or discarded.


The record of every count
The Count tab keeps score. Under Last counted, each type shows how long since it was counted. Under Record accuracy, every completed count is listed with how many products matched and what was short and over. With fewer than 8 counts, it’s a table; from 8, a chart shows each count’s match rate, with the range chance allows.
